# Copy to .env and adjust as needed. Compose reads .env automatically.
# These are dev-only placeholder values — never put real secrets here.

POSTGRES_USER=gameframework
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=gameframework
POSTGRES_DB=gameframework

# GF_DATABASE_URL is derived from the POSTGRES_* variables above by default,
# so there is a single source of truth for the password. It is what the
# backend app itself reads (pydantic-settings, env prefix GF_), what
# `alembic upgrade head` uses inside the container, and the one name the
# migration test suite (tests/db) reads too — the same variable everywhere,
# not a per-context alias. Only set it directly if you need to override the
# derived value.
# GF_DATABASE_URL=

# Uncomment and change if the default host ports are already taken on your
# machine. Postgres binds to localhost only by default; change
# POSTGRES_BIND_ADDRESS if you intentionally need it reachable from the LAN.
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# POSTGRES_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# BACKEND_PORT=8000
# FRONTEND_PORT=5173

# Required. The framework's own frontend origin — the only origin the API
# sends CORS headers for (never reflected, never wildcarded with
# credentials, ADR-0007). No default: an operator must set this to their
# real frontend origin, or the app refuses to start rather than silently
# accepting a documentation domain as a trusted CORS origin.
# GF_FRONTEND_ORIGIN=

# Required, no default. Directory the framework owns for files it writes and
# manages itself — currently the session-signing key, a 0600 file the framework
# draws from a CSPRNG at first start and rotates by itself at factory reset
# (ADR-0007). The key is never a value an operator supplies; the path is.
# There is no default because any default points inside the container: the key
# would land in the ephemeral layer, and every recreate would end every session
# at once — unnoticed at setup, noticed mid-event. Point this at a persistent
# path, or the app refuses to start. The filesystem there must also support
# hard links (os.link, used to publish the key safely) — most local and
# container-volume filesystems do; some NFS configurations do not.
# GF_DATA_DIR=

# Required, no default. The event domain the session cookie is scoped to
# (`Domain=`, ADR-0007, api-surface.md §2.2) — the same wildcard domain
# every minigame subdomain sits under. Give the bare domain, e.g.
# "event.example.com", with no leading dot: the framework strips one if
# present and emits exactly one itself, so this is the one place the
# wire form is decided rather than left to whichever way it was typed
# here. A constant standing in for this is worse than a missing setting —
# it would pin every installation to this document's example domain and
# emit a cookie no real deployment's browser keeps.
# GF_COOKIE_DOMAIN=

# Optional. The operator drop-in directory for community artifacts
# (minigames, events) an admin sideloads before the registry exists
# (data-model.md §3.26, api-surface.md §2.18) — one subdirectory per
# artifact, read at startup and on `POST /catalog/refresh`. Unlike
# GF_DATA_DIR/GF_FRONTEND_ORIGIN/GF_COOKIE_DOMAIN this is not required:
# it defaults to a "dropin" subdirectory of GF_DATA_DIR, which already
# sits inside the persistent data volume, so a drop-in placed there
# survives a container recreate by construction. Set this only if you
# want the drop-in directory to live somewhere else — e.g. a separate
# mounted artifact share.
# GF_DROPIN_DIR=

# Optional. Additional DNS labels, beyond the SDK's own floor ("callback"),
# that this installation has put a framework surface on under the event
# domain (sdk-contract-v1.md §3.4 check 14) — an event author's
# challenges[].minigame.host_label may not collide with one. Comma-separated,
# e.g. "app,admin". Defaults to empty: an installation naming none has,
# correctly, put no such surface up in M2, which ships no frontend.
# GF_RESERVED_HOST_LABELS=
